  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Tuning guitars + 'White Rabbit' (Jefferson Airplane)**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **Weeks Go By Like Days**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 5 archived performances [3]\n- Earliest performances in the archive: The Dark, One Big Holiday, I Will Sing You Songs, Lil Billy [3]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **mmj2000-01-29.aud.flac16** (recommended): audience recording; 11 songs; 70 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [1]. Said about its sound: Original info file calls it a very good audience recording [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Described as the earliest known audience-recorded My Morning Jacket performance [1]\n- Info file suggests it may be one of the group's earliest complete live recordings [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **mmj2000-01-29.aud.flac16**: taped by Erik V.; transferred by Magnix; source: AUD DAT > EasyTree BT > CD-R [1]. Also: Source chain given as audience DAT, then EasyTree BT, then CD-R; this copy ripped via EAC to FLAC level 8; In February 2005 the taper seeded it on easytree.org, marking the fifth anniversary of the 'From Nashville To Kentucky' website; Info file came with the BitTorrent release in February 2005, dedicated to Ger Potze, who maintains the MMJ website [1][2]",
